WEBVTT

00:00.450 --> 00:03.950
You've made the call.

00:03.950 --> 00:09.300
Someone you respect disagrees, strongly, and they're challenging your decision in front of other people.

00:09.300 --> 00:12.700
Before you respond, what do you notice?

00:13.200 --> 00:18.050
In your body, your thoughts, your feelings. What is your urge?

00:26.000 --> 00:31.050
Pressure changes when another person is involved.

00:31.050 --> 00:33.850
What is your first move? Options could be:

00:33.850 --> 00:36.200
Defend the decision.

00:36.200 --> 00:39.000
Back away from your position.

00:39.000 --> 00:43.400
Ask them to explain what you're missing.

00:43.400 --> 00:47.850
Pause, and separate the disagreement from the person.

00:55.650 --> 01:00.900
Now, same disagreement. This time, respond without defending yourself

01:00.900 --> 01:03.750
or abandoning your position.

01:07.900 --> 01:13.900
That's hard. And now you're conditioning alignment without commitment.

01:14.150 --> 01:19.650
This week, notice one moment when disagreement makes you want to defend,

01:19.650 --> 01:22.550
withdraw, or immediately solve.

01:22.550 --> 01:26.400
Catch the urge, then choose your response.
